# Generated artefacts must be LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# `tools/build-exports.mjs` writes LF unconditionally, and its `--check` mode
# compares bytes to decide whether the committed package is stale. On a Windows
# checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` git materialises CRLF, so the check reports
# files as stale that are byte-identical once line endings are normalised —
# while Linux CI sees nothing. Pinning eol=lf keeps generator, working tree and
# CI in agreement.
#
# Same reasoning as the Solidity rules in the repository-root .gitattributes;
# kept here so the contract toolchain owns its own artefacts.
exports/**/*.js    text eol=lf
exports/**/*.d.ts  text eol=lf
exports/**/*.json  text eol=lf
deployments/*.json text eol=lf
